From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: matthane <matthan.evans@icloud.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:42:40 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] VideoPlayer: open a prefetched add-on item's default streams
 early

A prefetched inputstream add-on item opens its streams only at the
join, where each fetches its first segments on connections the add-on
closed meanwhile. The join also ranks those streams before the item's
video settings load, with the settings of the item played before.
---
 .../include/kodi/addon-instance/Inputstream.h |  2 +-
 .../DVDInputStreams/InputStreamAddon.h        |  4 +-
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.cpp        | 66 ++++++++++++++++++-
 xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/VideoPlayer.h          |  2 +-
 4 files changed, 68 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/addons/kodi-dev-kit/include/kodi/addon-instance/Inputstream.h b/xbmc/addons/kodi-dev-kit/include/kodi/addon-instance/Inputstream.h
--- a/xbmc/addons/kodi-dev-kit/include/kodi/addon-instance/Inputstream.h
+++ b/xbmc/addons/kodi-dev-kit/include/kodi/addon-instance/Inputstream.h
@@ -0,7 +0,7 @@
 /// | <b>`point`</b> | The identification of the addon instance to inputstream is mandatory <b>`kodi.inputstream`</b>. In addition, the instance declared in the first <b>`<extension ... />`</b> is also
 /// | <b>`extension`</b> | A filename extension is an identifier specified as a suffix to the name of a computer file where supported by addon.
 /// | <b>`listitemprops`</b> | Values that are available to the addon at @ref InputstreamProperty::GetProperties() and that can be passed to @ref CInstanceInputStream::Open() ith the respective values.
-/// | <b>`prefetch`</b> | Optional, <b>`true`</b> if Kodi may open the next playlist item ahead of its playback, while another instance of the addon plays. Such an open is told by @ref InputstreamProperty::IsPrefetch().
+/// | <b>`prefetch`</b> | Optional, <b>`true`</b> if Kodi may open the next playlist item ahead of its playback, on another thread while another instance of the addon plays. Such an open is told by @ref InputstreamProperty::IsPrefetch(). Kodi may also open streams of that item before playback picks them. It opens each picked stream again before the first @ref CInstanceInputStream::DemuxRead(), and that repeated open of an enabled stream must change nothing. Streams playback does not pick are disabled with @ref CInstanceInputStream::EnableStream() before the first read or seek.
 /// | <b>`protocols`</b> | The streaming protocol is a special protocol supported by the addon for the transmission of streaming media data over a network.
 /// | <b>`library_@PLATFORM@`</b> | The runtime library used for the addon. This is usually declared by cmake and correctly displayed in the translated `addon.xml`.
 ///
diff --git a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/InputStreamAddon.h b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/InputStreamAddon.h
--- a/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/InputStreamAddon.h
+++ b/xbmc/cores/VideoPlayer/DVDInputStreams/InputStreamAddon.h
@@ -0,7 +0,9 @@
   ~CInputStreamAddon() override;
 
   static bool Supports(const ADDON::AddonInfoPtr& addonInfo, const CFileItem& fileitem);
-  // whether an instance may open ahead of playback, beside another open instance of the add-on
+  // whether an instance may open ahead of playback, on another thread beside an open instance of
+  // the add-on; its streams may open before the player claims them, and the player opens each
+  // claimed one again before its first read, which must then change nothing
   static bool SupportsPrefetch(const ADDON::AddonInfoPtr& addonInfo);
 
   void SetPrefetch(bool prefetch) { m_prefetch = prefetch; }
